  "notes": "Southern Province Cement Company (ticker 3050) audited financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/427_0_2026-04-07...). Auditor: BDO Dr. Mohamed Al-Amri & Co. The financial statements were approved by the Board of Directors on 30 March 2026. Amounts are presented in full Saudi Riyals (scale 1). The primary statements (printed FS pages 5-9) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.6x); the notes are digital text. These are the Company's standalone (non-consolidated) statements - Southern Province has no subsidiaries, hence no non-controlling interest and no consolidation. There are no discontinued operations - the standard pre-tax - zakat bridge applies. The FY2024 comparatives are RESTATED (issuer Note 34, the reclassification of investment properties). FY2025 was a LOSS year - a sharp jump in cost of revenues (from SAR 626.0m to SAR 835.2m as energy and clinker costs rose and prices fell) took gross margin from 33.0% to 3.7%, giving an operating loss of SAR 40.8m and a net loss of SAR 48.5m (FY2024 restated net profit SAR 193.0m); net_income, operating_income and FY2025 EPS (-0.35) are all negative and retained earnings fell to SAR 965.8m. impairment_charges is the '(Losses)/Reversal of Expected Credit Losses' line. other_reserves is the 'Statutory reserve' (SAR 700m, unchanged). income_taxes_and_zakat is the single 'Zakat' line - a SAR 13.5m charge against a pre-tax loss, so the effective-tax plausibility bound warns (expected). provisions is 'Quarry rehabilitation provision'. long_term_debt / current_debt are the non-current and current 'Bank borrowings'; other_current_liabilities is 'Dividend payables'; accrued_expenses is 'Accrued expenses and other current liabilities'; zakat_payable is 'Zakat provision'. FY2024 also carried a SAR 5.5m 'Investment properties' line (disposed in FY2025); it is not carried at FY2025. depreciation_amortization sums 'Depreciation on property, plant and equipment' and 'Amortization of intangible assets' from the cash-flow statement. capex is 'Additions of property, plant and equipment' (a heavy plant-upgrade year - SAR 657.8m, funded by SAR 624.3m of new loans). interest_paid is 'Finance costs paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat paid'; dividends_paid is 'Dividends paid'. The cash-flow closing balance equals the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line exactly. Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: financial position 6, profit or loss and OCI 7, changes in equity 8, cash flows 9.",
